  **B — Metadata.** `index.html` now has the default title, meta description, `theme-color: #0a1013`, and OG title/description/type/site_name/image (`lang="en"` was already there). Per-route titles via new `src/useDocumentTitle.ts` — verified live: `Fleet status — Is3` and `Architecture — Is3`.

  **C — Accessibility.** The big find: the skip-to-content link I added initially used a bare `href="#main-content"`, which **HashRouter intercepted as a route and blanked the page**. Caught by the keyboard probe, fixed by preventDefault + explicit focus/scroll. Verified over CDP with real key events:
  - Every one of 13+ Tab stops shows the 2px `--series-1` focus ring
  - Drawer traps Tab and Shift+Tab, closes on Esc, restores focus to the opening card
  - Heading order is clean h1→h2→h3(→h4) on both routes
  - Reduced motion neutralises the ping and all transitions (`1e-05s × 1`) while the feed keeps updating
  - Colour never carries meaning alone (icon + label + colour, plus height/opacity on the Pulse)

  **D — 360px.** One caveat worth knowing: Chrome headless clamps `--window-size` to a 500px minimum, so plain `--screenshot` at 360 produces a misleading clipped image. I switched to CDP device-metrics emulation: both routes measure `scrollWidth` exactly 360 with zero page-level overflow; only the wide tables/diagrams scroll deliberately inside their `overflow-x-auto` frames.

  **E — Deploy config.** `.github/workflows/deploy.yml` at the repo root (push to main + workflow_dispatch, correct permissions block, concurrency group, Node 20, `npm ci` + build in `frontend/`, upload-pages-artifact → deploy-pages), plus a root `.gitignore`. `base: './'` confirmed intact. No git operations performed.

  **F — Final verification.** `npm run build` exits 0, zero TS errors/warnings (73 modules, ~78 kB gzip JS). All four screenshots reviewed; console clean everywhere.

  Full write-up, including the a11y probe results and exact build output, is in `orchestration/logs/T6-SUMMARY.md`.

